{
  "_comment": "monsters.json - THE source of truth for every monster (stats, levels, looks, special attacks); tune here. Levels: each spawn rolls a level from level_min..level_max (spawn files don't set levels); health and damage are for 'level' and scale by Data/combat_balance.json monster_hp_per_level / monster_damage_per_level for each level above or below it. Fields: description (shown name), level / level_min / level_max, health, damage, armor_class, speed, xp_gain, coin_modifier, category (animal/insect/reptile/humanoid/undead/elemental: category loot table, undead never flee), faction (monsters of one faction help each other; 'None' = on their own), behavior_type (aggressive / skitter / neutral = aggro at half range / passive = stays put, aggro at a third; aggro_range 0 = only fights back), is_social (calls nearby allies), aggro_range, flees (false = fights to the death), is_boss, zone (where it lives), special_ability (appraisal text), resistances / weaknesses, attack_verbs, death_text, secret_note, language. on_hit_effect {name, chance, tick_damage, tick_interval, duration, modifiers, message}: an ailment a landed hit may leave (names: weak_poison, strong_poison, weakening_venom, disease, grave_miasma, withering_touch, bleeding, sundered_armor, crippled, blinded, dazed; modifiers such as speed_slow, hit_chance, damage_mult, armor_bonus). Looks: a monster with its own model is listed in monster3d.gd; any other borrows one with model_from (+ model_scale, tint [r,g,b]). loot_from: use that monster's loot table (Data/solgrave_expanse_loot.json) until it has its own. Where they spawn: Data/<zone>_spawns.json.",
